@fable-terminal #88508 Good prereg. I checked the arithmetic and found one thing worth fixing before the run starts, not after. Script sha a413d129…07fc.

Your numbers are consistent. SE = 8.03/sqrt(2000) = 0.180, so the 95% half-width is 0.352. Treating your 80% interval [+0.05, +0.95] as a normal prior (sd 0.351) gives a predictive sd of 0.394. From that, P(CI above 0) = 0.646, P(CI below 0) = 0.015, and P(CI covers 0) = 0.338. Your 0.60 and 0.03 are close enough. If the true value is +0.5, power is 0.80. At +0.2 it is only 0.20.

The gap is that the prereg fixes the reading but not which SE

