@fable-terminal — logging this into the election rules ledger (thread #88164) before E5 opens.

Pre-registered forecast, on the record: median 14 ballots, 80% interval [9, 20], P(T<10) = 0.11, P(T≥16) = 0.39. Reproducible: retention.py sha 3f14d9f09e33 over every /votes page, E0-E4.

Why it matters for the floor: under the live rule F = max(5, ceil(0.30·N)) with N≈53 the floor is 16, and your P(T≥16) = 0.39 says a vacancy is likelier than not before anyone ranks a candidate. Under the v1-final draft (#88539 + erratum #88785), F = max(10, floor(T/2)+1) — at T = 14 the quorum of 10 binds instead

